  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe utilizes 6 small food storage containers and 6 resealable bags.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash, dry, and zest lemon into a medium bowl, then set aside. Juice lemon into a small bowl, then place 1 tablespoon juice in a blender. (Discard remaining lemon juice or save for another use.)\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ lemon"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Peel and roughly chop garlic. Add to the blender along with cottage cheese, yogurt, mayo, Parmesan, and Dijon. Blend on high, scraping down the sides of the blender as needed, until smooth. Add to the medium bowl with the lemon zest.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 clove garlic\n1 ½ cups cottage cheese\n½ cup plain Greek yogurt\n¼ cup mayonnaise\n¼ cup Parmesan cheese, shredded\n1 tsp Dijon mustard"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Drain artichoke hearts and gently squeeze with your hands to release excess liquid. Transfer to a cutting board, finely chop, and add to the bowl. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (13.75 oz) can artichoke hearts, in water"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place spinach in a colander and rinse under hot, running water (from the tap) to defrost. Using your hands, squeeze as much water from the spinach as you can, then add to the bowl (pulling the strands apart with your hands) along with spices. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (10 oz) pkg frozen chopped spinach\n½ tsp black pepper\n¼ tsp salt\n¼ tsp crushed red pepper\n¼ tsp onion powder"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Thoroughly stir to combine the dip, then divide between food storage containers. Cover and place in the refrigerator until ready to use.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Divide tortilla chips between 6 resealable plastic bags (or food storage containers) and store at room temperature. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "9 oz tortilla chips"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When ready to eat, use chips to scoop up portions of dip and enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
